+## Individual review reasons
+
+- **#1 Steamrunner Class:** Affordable former fleet cruiser; slower handling and lighter weapons than the strike variant. Availability: general.
+- **#2 Excelsior Class:** Moves above Miranda in protection and cargo; no inherited Cutting Beam. Availability: general.
+- **#4 Nebula Class:** BM civilian conversion of a sensor-oriented cruiser; cargo and survey endurance offset slow handling and modest weapons. Availability: general.
+- **#9 Kingston Class:** Cargo and endurance upgrade; broad hull turns slowly and has one defensive beam. Availability: general.
+- **#10 Tug Class II:** Low-cost heavy lift with a real tractor, weak firepower and low impulse speed. Availability: general.
+- **#11 Vega Class:** Combat-focused civilian-market hull trades cargo and endurance for protection and agility. Availability: general.
+- **#15 Ambassador Civilian Refit:** Civilian Ambassador carries more freight but starts with much less armament than Imperial variant. Availability: general.
+- **#22 Delpin Warship:** Small Delpin combatant pays for dense defenses, compact weapons and high agility, not freight. Availability: general.
+- **#24 Lysian Fighter:** Cheapest fragile hull; all three empty slots remain armable. Availability: general.
+- **#25 Vulcan Warpship:** Useful defensive plasma beam and extra range above the basic Vulcan shuttle. Availability: general.
+- **#29 Romulan Scout:** Fast Romulan scouting and light attack; cloak requires a later larger hull or refit-compatible mass. Availability: general.
+- **#33 Akira Class:** Standard Akira keeps the lower swapped price; strike version adds protection and modern weapons. Availability: general.
+- **#35 Galaxy Class:** Galaxy earns its capital tier through shields, cargo and endurance rather than agility. Availability: general.
+- **#38 Sovereign Class:** Sovereign focuses on combat and speed; command variant trades some pace for endurance and cargo. Availability: general.
+- **#42 Neg'Var Warship:** Heavy Klingon assault hull; cloak and bulk offset poor turning and modest cargo. Availability: general.
+- **#47 Oberth Tug:** Oberth is the affordable tractor-equipped working ship below Nova survey capability. Availability: general.
+- **#48 Jem'Hadar Battlecruiser:** Heavy Dominion command ship; sold in the core, never the Blender remnant market. Availability: dominion-core.
+- **#49 Galaxy Dreadnaught:** Meaningful step above ordinary capitals while remaining below Excalibur; secret vendor retained. Availability: secret-paso; vendor paso-project-x.
+- **#50 Sentient Lifeform:** Unshielded organic transport trades combat capability for unusual endurance and cargo. Availability: general.
+- **#51 Delpin Luxury Liner:** Civilian liner has premium carrying capacity and protection, with empty armable slots. Availability: general.
+- **#53 Reman Warbird:** Reman stealth strike ship pays for cloak and Thaleron equipment; secret access remains. Availability: secret-remus; vendor remus-secret.
+- **#54 Tamarian Warship:** Balanced Tamarian hull is no longer priced below smaller escorts. Availability: general.
+- **#55 Alien Bioship:** High agility and unusual endurance justify a rare combat premium; tiny cargo prevents universal superiority. Availability: general.
+- **#60 Concord-class Grand Cruiser:** Concord preserves approved endgame values and commercial role; Excalibur retains superior combat durability. Availability: independent-endgame; vendor independent-endgame.
+- **#61 Klingon Qonos:** Armor-heavy flagship with limited cargo and slow handling; no routine ambient deployment. Availability: general.
+- **#62 Cardassian Behemoth:** Siege and logistics flagship trades speed for armor and freight; no routine ambient deployment. Availability: general.
+- **#64 Romulan Warhawk:** Shield-heavy stealth flagship with less total durability and cargo than universal old mega stats. Availability: general.
+- **#65 Dominion Battleship:** Heavy Dominion strength stays in the core or authorized deployments; expensive combat-focused flagship. Availability: dominion-core.
+- **#66 Tholian Conquest:** Slow shield-heavy command hull carries a tractor for web-like control, not huge generic cargo holds. Availability: general.
+- **#206 Dominion Scout:** Starter Dominion scout uses a compact legal weapon and prioritizes speed over durability. Availability: dominion-all.
+- **#207 Nausican Raider:** Powerful proton beam makes this raider an expensive specialist rather than a freighter bargain. Availability: general.
+- **#208 Venture Class:** Venture gains useful scout speed and modest protection without a massive accidental fuel reserve. Availability: general.
+- **#209 sydney Class:** Cargo and endurance justify Sydney pricing; modest protection and armament keep it below military cruisers. Availability: general.
+- **#210 Vulcan shuttle:** Basic logical transport starts unarmed and sits below the armed Warpship. Availability: general.
+- **#211 Vulcan Expeditionary Explorer:** Vulcan capital emphasizes shields, survey equipment and range, not fast assault. Availability: general.
+- **#212 Romulan Courier:** Cargo courier remains distinct from the faster and better-armed scout. Availability: general.
+- **#213 Imperial Class:** Imperial prioritizes armor and command-zone control over Galaxy cargo and survey endurance. Availability: general.
+- **#214 Freedom Class:** Low-cost civilian generalist trades combat protection for useful cargo and travel. Availability: general.
+- **#215 Tarellian Freighter:** Large hold and extended reserve are valuable; slow unarmed hull is vulnerable. Fuel-free travel is not implemented. Availability: general.
+- **#216 Dominion Cruiser:** Core combat cruiser is a genuine upgrade from the locally available attack ship. Availability: dominion-core.
+- **#217 Human Bird of Prey:** Mobile improvised warship pays for cloak and combat ability, sacrificing freight. Availability: general.
+- **#218 Breen Warship:** Breen combat fit includes engine disruption and heavy beam; clear military standing gate. Availability: general.
+- **#219 Son'a Warship:** Advanced subspace armament contributes materially to price and trust requirement. Availability: general.
+- **#220 Azuki:** Refitted multirole cruiser combines useful cargo with shielding and detection equipment. Availability: general.
+- **#221 Galaxy Command Variant:** Command Galaxy has stronger defenses and fleet-control fit than the standard explorer. Availability: general.
+- **#222 Tholian Shuttle:** Crystalline shuttle gets modest shields and a basic beam; heavy devices await a larger hull. Availability: general.
+- **#223 Tholian Cargo Ship:** Armored cargo platform gives up speed and heavy weapons for transport work. Availability: general.
+- **#224 Son'a Battleship:** Major battleship with expensive advanced fit, slow turning and limited commercial space. Availability: general.
+- **#225 Orion Starbridge:** Corrects the 520000 outlier; cloak and turret support a mid-tier private commerce ship. Availability: general.
+- **#226 Promelli Skiff:** Fast alien energy specialist is priced for its strong pulse weapon, not unexplained rarity alone. Availability: general.
+- **#227 Promelli Manitee:** Heavy alien energy fit and shielding distinguish it from the skiff; old near-million price removed. Availability: general.
+- **#228 Peregrin Fighter:** Peregrin specializes in short-range attack with little cargo and an expensive initial weapon fit. Availability: general.
+- **#229 Sovereign Yacht:** Sovereign yacht is a fast protected civilian craft; empty slots match its noncombat role. Availability: general.
+- **#230 Aurelius Patrol Frigate:** Patrol frigate pays for endurance and detection rather than cloak inherited from an unrelated item row. Availability: general.
+- **#231 Manticore Class:** Armor and twin quantum launchers make Manticore a dedicated assault hull with limited cargo. Availability: general.
+- **#232 Tholian Battleship:** Layered defenses and control equipment define a slow lane-holding battleship. Availability: general.
+- **#233 Breen Shuttle:** Cold-system courier carries a small disruptor; no invalid heavy turret or inherited cloak. Availability: general.
+- **#234 Breen Light Cruiser:** More shielding but less armor and freight than the larger Breen Warship. Availability: general.
+- **#235 Son'a Shuttle:** Fast support shuttle uses a compact pulse cannon rather than heavy subspace weapons. Availability: general.
+- **#236 Salcombe class :** Salcombe hauls construction material cheaply by sacrificing speed, maneuverability and combat equipment. Availability: general.
+- **#237 Vulcan Light Cruiser:** Fast defensive explorer exchanges armor and cargo for range and agility. Availability: general.
