+- **#287 Gagarin Class:** Gagarin emphasizes armor and sustained fleet attack, with shorter reach than survey peers. Availability: general.
+- **#288 Gorn Interceptor:** Reserved fast armored interceptor has reference stats but remains absent from normal markets and traffic. Availability: reserved-gorn.
+- **#289 Inquiry Class:** Inquiry is a modern frontline heavy ship; high protection and speed require a strategic gate. Availability: general.
+- **#290 Intrepid Frigate:** Early Earth Intrepid-pattern ship in civilian service; not a second Voyager-class explorer. Availability: general.
+- **#291 Kaplan F17 Freighter:** Kaplan F17 trades some bulk capacity for unusual freighter speed and useful range. Availability: general.
+- **#292 Cardassian Transport Ship:** Armored transport supports convoys; a limited beam fit and low speed keep it below war cruisers. Availability: general.
+- **#293 Kumari Class:** Kumari is a combat ship with pursuit and direct-fire emphasis, not a civilian hauler. Availability: general.
+- **#294 Luna Class:** Luna prioritizes survey endurance, supplies and shielding over a heavy primary weapon. Availability: general.
+- **#295 Norway Class:** Norway gets an escort-screen fit; its precise screen mission is not treated as canonical proof. Availability: general.
+- **#296 Orion Science Ship:** Civilian science vessel offers scanning and recovery equipment with a defensive turret. Availability: general.
+- **#297 Penine Class:** Affordable independent patrol craft favors protection over the Thawn's speed and stronger cannon. Availability: general.
+- **#298 Reliant Class:** Reliant trades peak combat output for cargo, a tractor and balanced patrol performance. Availability: general.
+- **#299 Sagan Class:** Sagan serves as a modern expedition capital; supplies and reach justify the price without assault specialization. Availability: general.
+- **#300 Sutherland Class:** Sutherland follows the sensor-oriented Nebula lineage, with modern shields and expedition capacity. Availability: general.
+- **#301 Thawn Class:** Fast independent escort pays for response speed and a pulse cannon, not copied cruiser stats. Availability: general.
+- **#302 Trieste Class:** Independent reconnaissance specialist trades heavy weapons and cargo for travel and agility. Availability: general.
+- **#303 Warp Delta:** Small Earth-derived fast craft has a patrol fit and limited expedition capacity. Availability: general.
+- **#305 Miranda Long-Range Frigate:** Miranda sits below Excelsior in price and protection, retaining a small endurance advantage. Availability: general.
+- **#306 Nova Surveyor:** Nova specializes in regional survey work; advanced endurance belongs to Intrepid and Luna. Availability: general.
+- **#307 Saber Planetary Defender:** Saber protects nearby systems; short range and tiny hold pay for strong light-ship defenses. Availability: general.
+- **#308 Danube Utility Runabout:** Danube is a useful armed small craft, below capital yachts in protection and capacity. Availability: general.
+- **#309 Deforest Armed Freighter:** Deforest combines trade and self-defense at a premium over slow dedicated haulers. Availability: general.
+- **#310 Aries Multipurpose Vessel:** Aries is a middle-of-the-road civilian hull with usable cargo and no specialist peak. Availability: general.
+- **#311 Mozart Civilian Explorer:** Mozart offers exploration reach before heavy protection; light armament keeps access civilian. Availability: general.
+- **#312 Centaur Reserve Cruiser:** Retired Centaur provides basic patrol protection below active Imperial cruiser capability. Availability: general.
+- **#313 Ambassador Imperial Cruiser:** Ambassador in Imperial service starts heavily armed and better protected than the civilian conversion. Availability: general.
+- **#314 Cardassian Hideki Shuttle:** Hideki is an armed patrol and attack craft despite the inherited shuttle name; not a cargo specialist. Availability: general.
+- **#315 Ferengi Marauder Refit:** Marauder is a well-protected armed trader; strong freight capability carries a real cost and trust gate. Availability: general.
+- **#316 Ferengi Cargo Shuttle:** Ferengi starter maximizes cheap hold space and begins unarmed, with all three slots still usable. Availability: general.
+- **#317 Ferengi Vagabond:** Vagabond protects trade routes through fast response and control equipment, sacrificing range and cargo. Availability: general.
+- **#318 Tholian Isaac Freighter:** Isaac is the best ordinary bulk hauler; slow travel and weak offensive fit preserve the escort need. Availability: general.
+- **#319 Delpin Long-Range Cruiser:** Long-range defensive cruiser extends beyond the smaller Delpin Warship's local combat role. Availability: general.
+- **#320 D'deridex Warbird:** D'deridex is a large deliberate warbird; protection, cloak and range outweigh speed and agility. Availability: general.
+- **#321 Norexan Warbird:** Norexan uses the Valdore-style fast warbird role; less durable than D'deridex but much more agile. Availability: general.
+- **#322 Jem'Hadar Attack Ship:** Compact armed Dominion attack ship remains the attainable Blender upgrade; larger strength is in the core. Availability: dominion-all.
+- **#323 Galor Cruiser:** Galor is an armored line cruiser with practical cargo; slower than sleek assault peers. Availability: general.
+- **#324 Keldon War Cruiser:** Keldon upgrades Galor protection and war fit while giving up some speed and agility. Availability: general.
+- **#325 Akira Strike Cruiser:** Upgraded Akira retains the approved higher swapped price and twin quantum launchers. Availability: general.
+- **#326 Defiant Escort:** Defiant keeps the approved price and pulse/quantum combat identity; cloak is optional, not standard to every hull. Availability: general.
+- **#327 Intrepid Explorer:** Intrepid earns its place through speed and deep-space endurance, not top assault protection. Availability: general.
+- **#328 Prometheus Tactical Cruiser:** Prometheus is a fast combat specialist; multivector separation is not implemented by this fit. Availability: general.
+- **#329 Sovereign Command Cruiser:** Sovereign command variant improves durability, cargo and endurance over the faster standard ship. Availability: general.
+- **#330 B'rel Scout:** B'rel is the stripped-down BM starter refit; its lack of a supplied cloak is a gameplay tier decision. Availability: general.
+- **#331 K't'inga Cargo Cruiser:** BM K't'inga cargo conversion retains basic Klingon defense but is explicitly not the standard battlecruiser role. Availability: general.
+- **#332 K'Vort Patrol Ship:** K'Vort adds protection, cloak and reach above the user-approved second-rung Bird of Prey. Availability: general.
+- **#333 Negh'Var Command Ship:** Command Negh'Var gains endurance and command-grade defenses without assuming a Dominion victory timeline. Availability: general.
+- **#334 Vor'cha Attack Cruiser:** Vor'cha balances assault armor with pursuit and cloak; inferior freight to armed haulers. Availability: general.
+- **#335 Akuzi Explorer:** Akuzi is a cheap explorer with weak defenses and light armament, below modern survey hulls. Availability: general.
+- **#336 New Orleans Civilian Refit:** New Orleans conversion trades the former military role for practical independent trade and escort work. Availability: general.
+- **#338 Tarellian Quantum Cruiser:** Tarellian cruiser trades peak combat output for extended reserve and cloak; literal fuel-free travel remains future work. Availability: general.
+- **#340 Constitution Utility Tug:** Retired cruiser tug is tough and roomy but slow, with only light self-defense and a working tractor. Availability: general.
+- **#341 Constellation Cargo Tug:** Larger cargo tug buys capacity and range at the cost of handling, shielding and weapons. Availability: general.
+- **#342 Olympic Support Ship:** Olympic supports evacuation and recovery with a utility-only fit; no automatic medical healing mechanic is claimed. Availability: general.
+- **#343 Vulcan C'Thia Defense Cruiser:** C'Thia holds territory with shielding and detection; less expedition cargo and reach than larger Vulcan explorers. Availability: general.
+- **#344 Steamrunner Strike Frigate:** Steamrunner strike variant retains its approved aggressive fit and outperforms the reserve hull in combat. Availability: general.
+- **#345 Bajoran Solar Sailor:** Fragile peaceful transport has cheap capacity and a generous reserve; sail refueling is not implemented here. Availability: general.
+- **#346 Borg Assimilation Cube:** Core Borg assault and assimilation platform; remains unavailable as ordinary civilian stock. Availability: borg-core.
+- **#347 Excalibur Class:** Excalibur retains the approved durability, price and 100 Terran gate; a game-specific Project X design. Availability: secret-paso; vendor paso-project-x.
+- **#348 Andorian Cargo Shuttle:** Cargo shuttle keeps its approved modest price and empty armable fit; less capacity than Ferengi, better mobility. Availability: general.
+- **#349 Utility Shuttle:** Unidentified utility design stays independent and affordable; no unsupported Andorian identity is invented. Availability: general.
+- **#350 Basic Shuttle:** Cheap entry transport remains empty but armable, with clear upgrades in cargo, protection and range. Availability: general.
+- **#351 Klingon Bird of Prey:** The user's second Klingon warship tier remains above B'rel and below K'Vort, larger than a shuttle. Availability: general.
+
+Role inspiration and uncertainties: [LORE-SOURCES.md](LORE-SOURCES.md). Numerical tuning and conversion choices are BM gameplay decisions.
