+# Lore and role review — 13 September 2026
+
+This is a Broken Mirror gameplay roster, not a canon fleet database. Approved
+factions, civilian conversions, artwork and distinct variants remain authoritative.
+Canonical classes inform roles; the prices, health, cargo, speed, standing and
+three-slot fits are authored game balance. The slots represent equipment groups,
+not a literal count of a starship's gun mounts.
+
+No authoritative class identification was found for many BM-specific names.
+Their original pack descriptions and the user's review govern those records.
+Names such as Concord, Delpin, Promelli, Thawn and the Project X Excalibur are
+not presented as newly verified canonical classes. The Excalibur supercapital is
+not the Ambassador- or Constitution-class ship that happens to share that name.
+The mixed-era imports remain deliberate BM adaptations; they do not establish
+that the canon timeline or BM2's Dominion-victory scenario happened in this game.
+
+## Sources and the actual decisions they informed
+
+| Source key | Evidence and application |
+|---|---|
+| `defiant` | StarTrek.com's official account identifies Defiant as a warship built against the Borg and describes its armor. #326 therefore emphasizes armor and compact combat capability. [Official Defiant history](https://www.startrek.com/en-un/news/celebrating-the-ships-of-the-line-uss-defiant-nx-74205). |
+| `starfleet-ak` | Akira's heavy armament, Ambassador's mixed scientific/combat role, and the Danube's transport role informed their fits. A cloaking device is not universal Defiant-class equipment; #326 now leaves its third slot open for player choice. Other modern-class roles are BM interpretations, not a claim that every profile has a canonical tactical specification. [EAS Starfleet A–K](https://www.ex-astris-scientia.org/schematics/starfleet_ships1.htm). |
+| `starfleet-lz` | Nebula has a sensor module; Nova is a small regional research vessel; Oberth is a science design; Olympic is a hospital/support design. Hence survey/logistics #4, regional survey #306, explicitly converted utility Oberth #47 and utility-only Olympic #342. Civilian tug conversions are BM decisions. Precise patrol assignments for sparsely described classes are not claimed as canon. [EAS Starfleet L–Z](https://www.ex-astris-scientia.org/schematics/starfleet_ships2.htm). |
+| `dominion` | The reference distinguishes a compact attack ship, a much larger battlecruiser and an exceptional battleship. This supports the size of the progression, not literal game damage numbers. Blender's remnant restriction and Dominica core distribution are the user's setting decisions. [EAS Dominion ships](https://www.ex-astris-scientia.org/schematics/dominion_ships.htm). |
+| `romulan` | D'deridex is a very large cloaked-warbird design; #320 favors protection and deliberate handling. Norexan is retained as the game's name for its approved Valdore-style design. The civilian/private conversions and separate BM cruiser names are adaptations. [EAS Romulan ships](https://www.ex-astris-scientia.org/schematics/romulan_ships.htm). |
+| `klingon` | The Bird-of-Prey and larger cruiser designs inform a combat-oriented ladder. The very weak #330 is explicitly a BM starter refit, not a claim that canonical B'rels lack warp or cloak. K't'inga #331 remains the approved cargo conversion, distinguished from its battlecruiser lineage. [EAS Klingon ships](https://www.ex-astris-scientia.org/schematics/klingon_ships.htm). |
+| `cardassian` | Hideki is used for patrol/attack despite shuttle terminology; Galor is a cruiser and Keldon develops its frame. #314 is armed, and #324 is a more capable war cruiser above #323. [EAS Cardassian ships](https://www.ex-astris-scientia.org/schematics/cardassian_ships.htm). |
+| `vulcan` | Vulcan references include both science and combat cruisers and support craft. They support a varied defensive/exploration ladder, not assigning every ring-shaped render to a named canonical class. The user's #211 and C'Thia identities stay intact. [EAS Vulcan ships](https://www.ex-astris-scientia.org/schematics/vulcan_ships.htm). |
+| `lower-decks` | California is a support vessel used for second contact, salvage and engineering. Parliament is a larger Starfleet design; its advanced operations fit here is a BM role choice inspired by the Vancouver, not a new universal canon specification. [EAS Lower Decks fleet](https://www.ex-astris-scientia.org/schematics/low_federation.htm). |
+| `early-earth` | The early Intrepid type is distinct from Voyager's class. #290 is described as an early Earth-pattern civilian refit, and #327 remains the later explorer. Old NX/Daedalus and Warp Delta conversions remain gameplay choices. [EAS early Earth ships](https://www.ex-astris-scientia.org/schematics/prefed_ships.htm). |
+| `hirogen` | The hunter ship's protected hull and the larger Venatic support an armored hunting ladder. This does not identify every BM Hirogen render as that exact class. [EAS Delta Quadrant F–K](https://www.ex-astris-scientia.org/schematics/delta_ships2.htm). |
+| `ferengi` | D'Kora combines trading and warship capability. #315 therefore keeps substantial freight capacity and a serious defensive fit, instead of becoming either a helpless freighter or a cargo-free battleship. [EAS Ferengi ships](https://www.ex-astris-scientia.org/schematics/ferengi_ships.htm). |
+| `crossfield` | Crossfield is an experimental design. #265 is given a research/transit role; the documented spore-drive history is not implemented as an ability. [EAS Discovery-era fleet](https://www.ex-astris-scientia.org/schematics/discovery_federation.htm). |
+| `bm-source-and-user-review` | The supplied BM1/BM2 descriptions and approved hull/duplicate decisions govern game-specific designs and conversions. Every original description is preserved in the record's `balanceReview.sourceDescription`; authored current descriptions describe the configured ship. |
+
+EAS is a secondary reference with its own interpretations; uncertain details
+are not elevated to official canon. No artwork was downloaded from these sources.
+
+## Mechanics deliberately not promised by a role label
+
+- Science equipment here means available tachyon/utility equipment and travel
+  capacity, not a new science mission or sensor simulation.
+- An Olympic does not automatically heal ships. A tractor-equipped hull does
+  have the existing tractor device. No carrier launch system was added.
+- Crossfield has no spore drive and Prometheus has no multi-vector separation.
+- Extended reserves on organic, quantum-drive and sailing ships do not mean
+  free antimatter or passive refueling. Those abilities need a separate patch.
+- The existing weapon catalog provides the three-slot abstractions. Its weapon
+  names and damage figures were not rewritten to claim canon accuracy.
